# matchdb is NOT read by this script and nothing was installed during the run.
#
# WHAT MOVED, 0.1.6 -> 0.1.8 (K1 is hand-rolled and normalizer-independent, so
# its row is identical, which is the control):
#   K2 groups           1,941,116 -> 1,940,724   (-392)
#   K3 groups           1,939,261 -> 1,939,261   (identical, and necessarily so:
#                         K3 strips all spaces, so it cannot see whether a
#                         hyphen became a space or nothing -- an internal check
#                         that the run is measuring what it claims)
#   K1 -> K2 splits     1,612 (0.08%) -> 1,482 (0.07%)
#   K2 merges >1 K1     87,790 (4.53%) -> 87,928 (4.54%)
#   K3 merges >1 K2     2,278 (0.12%) -> 1,886 (0.10%)
#   of those, street_num disagrees   972 (42.67%) -> 322 (17.07%)
#
# READ THE LAST LINE AGAINST THE LOCAL CASE AGAINST K3, NOT FOR IT. The 0.1.6
# figure is what this repo rejected K3 on. 17.07% is a materially better trade
# than 42.67%, so our own evidence against K3 is now WEAKER than it was. The
# rejection stands on the upstream 22,026,817-row measurement of the narrow
# variant instead (92,797 street-name strings moved, 17,614 of them
# unresolvable), which is stronger than anything this file can show. Said
# plainly in dev/PLACES-SYNC.md section 4 step 4 rather than left for a reader
# to notice.
